# L §4.5 Whatever a version states is read as its rows are, L §5.19 Coverage, E §4.1 step 3 (tally 2.1.8 R12, #182; the
# plan's c4): an observation dated on K or later is seen but not applied, and so is the link it states: the plan
# instance it fulfils stays booked. With on = 2026-04-10, pay[2026-04] (1 000.00 PLN on the 10th) is booked, the row
# of that day isn't: konto 2 000.00 PLN on 04-30 (b), flows(pay) 1 000.00 PLN (f), one movement (c). 2.1.7's refcore
# took the instance out of the plan for the row and booked neither: 1 000.00 and 950.00 PLN.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input amt: money PLN
input dom: int

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 1000.00 PLN "s"
  dom = 10 "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-04
  known 2026-04-10
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-04-10, kind: transfers, leg cash from world to konto amount 950.00 PLN, fulfils: pay[2026-04]) "r"

ask b: bal(konto, 2026-04-30), bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
ask f: flows(pay, 2026-04-01 .. 2026-04-30)
ask c: count(t in transfers over 2026-04)
=== expect
b: (2 000.00 PLN, 1 000.00 PLN)
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-03]
  cut 2026-04-10
c: 1
  cut 2026-04-10
f: 1 000.00 PLN
  cut 2026-04-10
